<h2>Evidence record</h2>

<p>The signature component. A grade — confidence tag plus basis, from
<code>{% raw %}{% grade %}{% endraw %}</code> — sits in the rail; the bare value and a
plain-language label sit in the main column.</p>

<ol class="record-list evidence">
    <li class="record evidence__item" data-confidence="exact">
        <div class="evidence__grade">{% grade "golden_dataset_india_mh" %}</div>
        <div>
            <p class="evidence__value">{% metric "golden_dataset_india_mh" %}</p>
            <p class="evidence__label">Golden-dataset cases gating every India Maternal Health release</p>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li class="record evidence__item" data-confidence="estimate">
        <div class="evidence__grade">{% grade "anomaly_sampling_yield" %}</div>
        <div>
            <p class="evidence__value">{% metric "anomaly_sampling_yield" %}</p>
            <p class="evidence__label">More judge-worthy edge cases surfaced per week, same cost</p>
        </div>
    </li>
</ol>

<h3>Evidence record, three abreast</h3>

<p>The <code>evidence--columns</code> modifier, as the homepage uses it. The
grade moves below the figure and the rail becomes a stack, because a third of
the band has no room for a label beside a 42px value.</p>

<p>It is a modifier and not the default for a reason this page proved: applied
to <code>.evidence</code> itself, the long estimate above rendered seven
characters to the line in a 285px column and ran 1,882px tall. Short figures
only.</p>

<ol class="record-list evidence evidence--columns">
    <li class="record evidence__item" data-confidence="exact">
        <div class="evidence__figure">
            <p class="evidence__value">{% metric "golden_dataset_india_mh" %}</p>
            <p class="evidence__label">Golden-dataset cases gating every India Maternal Health release</p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence__grade">{% grade "golden_dataset_india_mh" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="record evidence__item" data-confidence="exact">
        <div class="evidence__figure">
            <p class="evidence__value">{% metric "languages" %}</p>
            <p class="evidence__label">Languages the platform answers in</p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence__grade">{% grade "languages" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="record evidence__item" data-confidence="approximate">
        <div class="evidence__figure">
            <p class="evidence__value">{% metric "nightly_eval_cost" %}</p>
            <p class="evidence__label">Cost of the full nightly evaluation run</p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence__grade">{% grade "nightly_eval_cost" %}</div>
    </li>
</ol>

<h2>Gate</h2>

<p>The secondary motif. A result and the limitation beside it, always paired and
always named in text — colour is reinforcement, never the only signal.</p>

<div class="gate">
    <div class="gate__item gate__item--pass">
        <p><span class="gate__tag">Pass</span> Clinical Safety PASS rate reached
        {% metric "clinical_safety_pass" %} after the danger-sign fix shipped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="gate__item gate__item--fail">
        <p><span class="gate__tag">Fail</span> {% metric "annotation_override_rate" %} — the
        judge is still too conservative on non-urgent symptom mentions.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2>Numbered list</h2>

<p>For genuinely sequential or ranked content — the homepage's selected work, the
archive's dated entries. Not used for anything that is not actually a sequence.</p>

<ol class="numbered-list">
