<h2>Table</h2>

<p>Tables are wrapped at build time in a focusable, labelled scroll region, so a
table wider than a phone is reachable by keyboard. This one is deliberately wide
enough to overflow at the narrow viewport.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Approach</th>
            <th scope="col">What it catches</th>
            <th scope="col">What it misses</th>
            <th scope="col">Cost per run</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>Threshold gate</td>
            <td>A regression past a fixed line</td>
            <td>Slow drift underneath the line</td>
            <td>Low</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Trend view</td>
            <td>Drift, and the shape of it over time</td>
            <td>Nothing, but it does not block a merge</td>
            <td>Storage and a dashboard</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Code block</h2>

<p>A <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> gets <code>tabindex="0"</code> from the same
transform, for the same reason.</p>

<pre><code>eleventyConfig.addTransform("scrollableRegions", function (content) {
    if (!this.page.outputPath || !this.page.outputPath.endsWith(".html")) return content;
    let tableIndex = 0;
    return content.replace(/&lt;table\b[^&gt;]*&gt;/g, (openTag) =&gt; { /* … */ });
});</code></pre>

