<h2>Test-lab result</h2>

<p>The parts of <a href="{{ '/lab/' | url }}">the test lab</a> that hold still.
The panel itself is not here: its output depends on a test run and its
durations change every time, so a screenshot of it would fail every baseline
for reasons that have nothing to do with design. The step rows and the verdict
are the components carrying the new CSS, and they are deterministic, so they
are what gets covered.</p>

<p>The status is a word before it is a colour. A row that signalled pass and
fail only by hue would be two identical rows to a colour-blind reader, and
unreadable in a screenshot diff — which is where these are mostly looked at.</p>

<p class="lab-verdict is-pass">Solved. Assert on the state the user would see,
not on the fact that you performed an action.</p>

<section class="lab-run is-pass">
    <h3 class="lab-run__title">Run 1 · default — pass <span>(412ms)</span></h3>
    <ol class="lab-steps">
        <li class="lab-step is-pass">
            <span class="lab-step__title">click getByTestId("approve")</span>
            <span class="lab-step__ms">138ms</span>
        </li>
        <li class="lab-step is-pass">
            <span class="lab-step__title">expect(getByTestId("status")).toHaveText("approved 1")</span>
            <span class="lab-step__ms">54ms</span>
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>

<p class="lab-verdict is-fail">Not yet — 2 of 3 runs failed. A test that passes
sometimes is a test that fails sometimes.</p>

<section class="lab-run is-fail">
    <h3 class="lab-run__title">Run 2 · flaky — fail <span>(5204ms)</span></h3>
    <ol class="lab-steps">
        <li class="lab-step is-pass">
            <span class="lab-step__title">waitForTimeout(200)</span>
            <span class="lab-step__ms">201ms</span>
        </li>
        <li class="lab-step is-fail">
            <span class="lab-step__title">expect(getByTestId("answer")).toContainText("anomaly scan")</span>
            <span class="lab-step__ms">5001ms</span>
            <pre class="lab-step__error">Timed out 5000ms waiting for expect(getByTestId("answer")).toContainText("anomaly scan")
  Expected: "anomaly scan"
  Received: "Loading review…"</pre>
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>
